course: dictionary
lesson: 3573
title: Feuds: long, bitter quarrels
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A feud is a long, bitter quarrel between two people, families or groups. It does not end after one argument. It can carry on for years, sometimes for many generations. «The two families feuded for years.» Here feuded is the verb: they kept on quarrelling for a very long time.
explain: Look at the words around feud to work out its meaning. «A family feud» tells you it is a quarrel within a family. «A bitter feud» tells you the quarrel is full of anger and hurt. «End a feud» tells you a feud can stop, and that stopping it takes effort from someone.
explain: Feuds can also be made-up or friendly. «A joke feud, like a cooking contest between neighbours, is fine as long as everyone is in on the joke.» The clue is in the words in on the joke: everyone knows it is pretend, so nobody is really hurt.
fact: A feud is a long, bitter quarrel between people, families or groups.
fact: Feud can be a noun (a feud) or a verb (to feud).
fact: Famous feuds in stories and history include the Hatfields and McCoys in the USA and the Montagues and Capulets in «Romeo and Juliet».
fact: A feud can keep going when people take revenge, and it can end when someone makes a kind move, like «bringing soup to someone ill».
fact: Children are often caught in the middle of grown-ups' feuds, even though they did nothing wrong, and it is fine to tell a parent honestly how that makes you feel.
exercise: «One kind act, like bringing soup to someone ill, can end a feud.» What does end a feud mean? | Start a brand new quarrel | Cook a big dinner for the whole street | *Bring the quarrel to an end | Make the quarrel last even longer
exercise: «The two families feuded for years.» What does feuded mean here? | Went on a long holiday together | Shared one house for many years | Painted their fences the same colour | *Had a long, bitter quarrel
exercise: «A joke feud, like a cooking contest between neighbours, is fine as long as everyone is in on the joke.» What makes a joke feud fine? | Nobody knows it is a contest | It goes on for many generations | The neighbours are angry and bitter | *Everyone knows it is pretend
test: What is a feud? | A kind gift for a friend | A quick game of tag in the playground | A sweet cake shared at a party | *A long, bitter quarrel between people or groups
test: «Children are often caught in the middle of grown-ups' ___, even though they did nothing wrong.» Which word fits? | *feuds | puddles | garden | smiles
exam: Which of these shows a feud coming to an end? | Two families argue again at every meal | The quarrel grows bigger every single year | Cousins keep the quarrel alive for generations | *Neighbours bring soup to each other and make up
